# Conventional Commits format: <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# To use this template automatically: git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Types: feat | fix | chore | docs | refactor | test | ci | perf | style | revert | build
#
# Scopes for this repository:
#   repo         - root configuration, tooling, governance
#   infra        - docker-compose, MinIO, environment setup
#   api          - NestJS backend application
#   web          - Next.js frontend application
#   vault        - vault browse/download/delete/copy routes
#   uploads      - single/multipart/stream upload routes
#   signed       - presigned URL routes and direct upload flow
#   validation   - MIME/size/magic-byte validation pipeline
#   scanner      - file scanner adapter and verdict routes
#   tenants      - key-prefix isolation and tenant management
#   errors       - error demo routes and exception filter
#   system       - health, config introspection, provider recipes
#   ci           - GitHub Actions workflows
#   docs         - documentation files
#   test         - test infrastructure and suites
#
# Rules:
#   - Subject line: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period, <=72 chars
#   - Body: wrap at 100 chars; explain WHY, not WHAT
#   - No Co-Authored-By or AI-attribution lines
#
